        "id": 2903
      },
      "writtenOn": "2014-06-04T06:08:37Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Refresh has extra overhead: it would make the same call a get would make to the DB. This is a case of trying to avoid incurring an extra DB call with no direct reason to.\n\nThere is little reason to pre-seed the cache in this case as the next call to the get method will seed the cache. Updates do not necessitate a subsequent operation, sometimes an update is just an update.",
      "parentUuid": "1ae5cdf2_19379a4f",
      "revId": "c4b5d396365b02f7abe62c95a01ed90fc94674f2",
      "serverId": "4a232e18-c5a9-48ee-94c0-e04e7cca6543",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1ae5cdf2_1b52b766",
        "filename": "keystone/assignment/core.py",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 102,
      "author": {
        "id": 1091
      },
      "writtenOn": "2014-06-05T18:59:44Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, not every update needs to be followed by get call. I was trying to follow the pattern where in above create_project logic, the entity is pushed into cache after driver create call. Instead of refresh, other option is to call \u0027set\u0027 as latest data (\u0027ret\u0027) is already read from DB. This can be useful for subsequent gets.",
      "parentUuid": "1ae5cdf2_2b9e8a07",
      "revId": "c4b5d396365b02f7abe62c95a01ed90fc94674f2",
      "serverId": "4a232e18-c5a9-48ee-94c0-e04e7cca6543",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1ae5cdf2_87d009cb",
        "filename": "keystone/assignment/core.py",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 102,
      "author": {
        "id": 2903
      },
      "writtenOn": "2014-06-06T18:08:41Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I found that create usually is followed by a get. Updates less so.\n\nAlso, in this case use of .set() would be better than .refresh. refresh would call back to the DB for no reason. The benefit of the pre-seeding of the cache is negligible in most cases and I could argue to remove it from the .create calls for roughly the same reasons as I\u0027m not using it here.\n\nThe first .get will populate the cache and in most cases is sufficient (even under high load) to increase performance noticeably.\n\nIn either case, if we are making a change from .invalidate to .set or .refresh, I\u0027d like it separate from this bug fix.",
      "parentUuid": "1ae5cdf2_1b52b766",
      "revId": "c4b5d396365b02f7abe62c95a01ed90fc94674f2",
      "serverId": "4a232e18-c5a9-48ee-94c0-e04e7cca6543",
